  "raw_response": "`REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` is read during environment-setting merge, but an explicit `verify=False` is preserved and ultimately disables certificate verification.\n\nRelevant files:\n\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:src/requests/sessions.py?L750-L779](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/src/requests/sessions.py?L750-L779) - Reads `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` (then `CURL_CA_BUNDLE`) only when the request-level `verify` is `True` or `None`; merges the result with `self.verify`.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:src/requests/sessions.py?L265-L274](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/src/requests/sessions.py?L265-L274) - Sends the resolved `verify` value through the adapter.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:src/requests/adapters.py?L304-L340](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/src/requests/adapters.py?L304-L340) - `verify=False` selects `CERT_NONE` and clears CA bundle settings; a bundle path selects `CERT_REQUIRED`.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:tests/test_requests.py?L953-L984](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/tests/test_requests.py?L953-L984) - Tests environment bundle precedence and fallback behavior.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:docs/user/advanced.rst?L238-L252](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/docs/user/advanced.rst?L238-L252) - Documents CA-bundle environment variables and `verify=False`.",
